  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-08T21:48:16.055Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As an avatar creator, it is very difficult to show people my avatars when I don't know if they have it shown or not, and usually, going up to people and going \"hey, show my avatar\" usually doesn't work. Not knowing if people can see my avatar really demotivates me to make and show off my avatars, because what's the point if no-one can see it?\nSo, I suggest having a little eye icon under the nameplate (similar to the hand icon for when a user has physbones interaction on) that shows if a user has your avatar FULLY shown. If not, maybe have an icon of the eye crossed out or something like that.\nI think this could help out all avatar creators who want to show off their cool animations to people they don't know. If the avatar isn't working for the other person, they can just look at the icon and go \"oh yeah you don't have my avatar shown\" instead of having the other person fiddle around with their safety settings and being confused as to why it's not working. This could overall make showing off avatars a much smoother experience.\nThanks for reading :)",
